  "description": "NAMHER crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H88 Gd6 N10 O32. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1D (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2D (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3D (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.568-4.014 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.88-114.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C78H88Gd6N10O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
